    np:hasAssertion sub:assertion ;
    np:hasProvenance sub:provenance ;
    np:hasPublicationInfo sub:pubinfo .
}

sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/hypothesis/exocoetidae-substitution-budget> a delphi:Hypothesis, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Substitution budget of the flying-fish lineage (Exocoetidae) over its fossil duration, from the machine-checked fixation theorems: inconclusive for the gliding-to-flight question" ;
    dct:description "Over the 48.07 to 56 million years since the oldest Exocoetidae fossil, the machine-checked fixation theorems give the lineage a neutral substitution budget of 0.053 to 0.451 substitutions per site (5.50e+7 to 4.69e+8 genome-wide), independent of population size; adaptive substitutions have a floor of mu_f T per site that depends on an undefined favored-mutation rate, and a ceiling of 2 N mu T per site that is vacuous. Whether this was enough to modify a gliding fish into a winged animal (Darwin 1859, ch. VI) is inconclusive: the number of substitutions a wing requires is not a defined quantity, so there is nothing to compare the budget with." ;
    delphi:context "Darwin, On the Origin of Species (1859), chapter VI: flying-fish \"might have been modified into perfectly winged animals\" (Project Gutenberg text 1228, lines 5639-5642; organisms/darwin-origin/ch05-06/mentions.json). Taxon: Exocoetidae, NCBI Taxonomy 76072, GBIF 2968, Wikidata Q183686, PBDB txn:266181. Parameters and sources: Paleobiology Database, data service 1.2, taxa/single for Exocoetidae with show=app: first appearance 56 to 48.07 Ma (Ypresian), 7 occurrences; oldest occurrence Rhamphexocoetus volans, Early Eocene (Monte Bolca). FishBase species summary for Hirundichthys affinis (fourwing flyingfish, Exocoetidae): \"Generation time: 0.6 ( na - na) years. Estimated as median ln(3)/K based on 1 growth studies\" and \"max. reported age: 1.00 years (Ref. 6503)\". Chang, Yuan, Hoyle, Farley and Shiao (2022). Growth parameters and spawning season estimation of four important flyingfishes in the Kuroshio Current off Taiwan. Front. Mar. Sci. 8:747382. Sex-combined von Bertalanffy K between 3.534 and 4.350 per year for Cypselurus poecilopterus, Hirundichthys oxycephalus, Cheilopogon atrisignis and Cheilopogon unicolor; no age at maturity or generation time reported. Feng, Pettersson, Lamichhaney, Rubin, Rafati, Casini, Folkvord and Andersson (2017). Moderate nucleotide diversity in the Atlantic herring is associated with a low mutation rate. eLife 6:e23907. Pedigree estimate 2.0e-9 per site per generation, 95% CI 1.1e-9 to 2.9e-9. Zhang, Reid, Sands, Fraimout, Schierup and Merila (2023). De novo mutation rates in sticklebacks. Mol. Biol. Evol. 40:msad192. Pedigree estimates 4.83e-9 and 4.29e-9 per base per generation in two marine populations of Pungitius pungitius. Xu, Zhao, You, Yang, Chen, Ruan, Gu, Xu, Bian and Shi (2021). Draft genome of the mirrorwing flyingfish (Hirundichthys speculiger). Front. Genet. 12:695700. \"We obtained a 1.04-Gb genome assembly\". Exocoetus volitans: more than 1e9, effective population size from Bayesian demographic modelling of cytochrome b mtDNA (1106 bp, n = 266), described in the abstract as having increased ~150,000 years ago \"to more than 1 billion individuals currently\"; Lewallen, Bohonak, Bonin, van Wijnen, Pitman and Lovejoy (2016). Population genetic structure of the tropical two-wing flyingfish (Exocoetus volitans). PLoS ONE 11:e0163198. Caveats: A fossil first appearance is a minimum age for the lineage; the crown group may be older, which would only raise the budget. The Ypresian occurrence is dated to an interval, so both ends are carried. Darwin's sentence looks forward from gliding to flight; the elapsed duration is the only measured span available, so the budget is what this lineage has already had, not what the transition would get. The 56 to 48.07 Ma first appearance rests on two occurrence records from one publication (Bannikov 2014, Monte Bolca); the next-oldest record is 37.71 to 33.9 Ma (David 1946). The hub's visuals agent found that 3 of 12 PBDB first-appearance dates it checked for other taxa were database errors (genus-name homonyms, a contradicted genus record), so a single-source date deserves a sensitivity row; nothing suggests the Bannikov records are wrong. The sensitivity case uses the late end of the alternative record, 33.9 Ma, as T is linear in the duration. One species has a generation-time estimate, and it is a FishBase formula from one growth study. No family-wide value exists. The range 0.6 to 1.0 year follows the two FishBase numbers; a 2-year sensitivity case is reported separately because larger Cheilopogon species may live longer than Hirundichthys affinis, and no source was found that measures it. No mutation-rate estimate exists for any Exocoetidae. Both sources are pedigree estimates in other teleost orders; the range is the lowest confidence bound to the highest point estimate among them. Assembly size, not the callable or functional fraction. The per-genome numbers are an upper envelope on sites, not a count of sites that matter for a wing. Poorly constrained for the family. The ceiling is therefore reported as a function of N; the neutral budget and the floor do not depend on N (that is the content of the theorem)." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/exocoetidae-substitution-budget-computation> ;
    prov:used <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/favored-fixation-lower-bound>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/kimura-substitution-rate>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/kimura-fixation-probability>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/dataset/pbdb-occurrence-counts-2026-10-31> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.23907>, <https://doi.org/10.1093/molbev/msad192>, <https://doi.org/10.3389/fgene.2021.695700>, <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0163198>, <https://doi.org/10.3389/fmars.2021.747382>, <https://paleobiodb.org/data1.2/taxa/single.json?name=Exocoetidae&show=app>, <https://www.fishbase.se/summary/7457> ;
    skos:scopeNote "Kernel-checked: Delphi.FavoredChain.fixationProbability_ge: in an absorbing chain on 0..M copies whose expected copy number never decreases (selection neutral or for the mutant), with positive one-step escape from every interior state, a lineage of i copies fixes with probability at least i/M; the limit exists because fixation is absorbing." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Kernel-checked: Delphi.wrightFisherSelection_fixation_one_ge: Wright-Fisher sampling with mutant relative fitness 1+s, s >= 0, is such a chain, so one new mutant fixes with probability at least 1/M." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Kernel-checked: Delphi.neutral_expectedSubstitutions: with the proved neutral fixation probability 1/M, the defined expected count M mu u T equals mu T for every M." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Kernel-checked: Delphi.favored_expectedSubstitutions_ge and Delphi.expectedSubstitutions_le: for any favored chain mu T <= M mu u T, and for any u <= 1, M mu u T <= M mu T." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Assumed, not proved: The expected count M mu u T is a definition (Kimura 1968: new mutants per generation times fixation probability, summed over generations). Independent fates, no linkage or interference, constant M, constant mu, constant s and non-overlapping generations enter through that definition and are not proved." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Assumed, not proved: The numbers for T, mu, G and N come from the literature sources named in lean/bound/parameters.json, none of which measures Exocoetidae for mu or generation time; the fossil first appearance is a minimum age, and it rests on two PBDB occurrence records from one publication (Bannikov 2014, Monte Bolca); the next-oldest record (David 1946) is 37.71 to 33.9 Ma and is carried as a sensitivity case." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Assumed, not proved: The selection coefficient, the fraction of mutations selection favours, and the number of substitutions a wing requires are undefined; the result is a one-sided budget with nothing to compare it to." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Assumed, not proved: Nothing here is about which substitutions, in which genes, or whether they are reachable in sequence; a count of fixations is not a path to a wing." ;
    rdfs:comment "Verdict: inconclusive. The quantity the budget would have to be compared with, the number of substitutions a wing requires, is undefined; no figure is invented. The floor on adaptive substitutions also depends on the undefined fraction of mutations that selection favours. What is established: the neutral budget and the floor do not depend on N (the parameter the literature constrains least), and the ceiling is vacuous. Does not establish: that a wing was or was not reachable; which genes or substitutions a wing needs; that any of the named parameters hold for Exocoetidae (none of mu, generation time or N is measured for the family, and the fossil age is a minimum); anything beyond the Wright-Fisher model with independent mutant fates. The arithmetic multiplying the proved rate by generations and sites is a definition applied with a script (lean/bound/compute.mjs), kernel-checked only in the form of the theorems named above. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated. The dataset IRI <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/dataset/pbdb-occurrence-counts-2026-10-31> follows the Delphi dataset convention for the repository record organisms/darwin-origin/ch05-06/datasets/pbdb-occurrence-counts-2026-10-31.json; its dataset nanopub is unpublished at build time." ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/organism-blueprint-a-flying-fish> ;
    rdfs:comment "Related record: <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/organism-blueprint-a-flying-fish> is the organism thread's ontology-derived anatomical blueprint for the living family (organism-design/nanopubs/unsigned/claim-blueprint-a-flying-fish.trig, delphi:hypothesisType ontology-derived design proposal, 13 organ systems, 67 organs, 198 tissues and 257 cell types as distinct terms, confirmed by the organism thread 2026-10-31). The two records are independent statements about the same taxon; this is a citation, not a support or derivation relation in either direction. Neither record is evidence about the transition Darwin imagined." ;
    dct:references "darwin-origin/inputs/pg1228.txt#line=5639,5642" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/4ebb56add61de66744fe8b957ecd7c0bcecc8083/lean/bound/parameters.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/4ebb56add61de66744fe8b957ecd7c0bcecc8083/lean/bound/compute.mjs>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/4ebb56add61de66744fe8b957ecd7c0bcecc8083/lean/Delphi/Favored.lean>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/4ebb56add61de66744fe8b957ecd7c0bcecc8083/organisms/darwin-origin/ch05-06/taxa/exocoetidae.json>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/lean.json>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/#flyingfish> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/exocoetidae-substitution-budget-computation> a delphi:EvidenceItem ;
    rdfs:label "Computation of the Exocoetidae substitution budget from the audited theorems and the sourced parameters" ;
    dct:description "Theorems (all accepted by Lean leanprover/lean4:v4.35.0 with standard axioms only; see lean.json audit): Delphi.neutral_expectedSubstitutions [E[substitutions] = mu * T for the neutral Wright-Fisher chain, every M]; Delphi.favored_expectedSubstitutions_ge [mu * T <= E[substitutions] for any favored chain (expected copy number never decreases)]; Delphi.expectedSubstitutions_le [E[substitutions] <= M * mu * T for any fixation probability u <= 1]; Delphi.wrightFisherSelection_fixation_one_ge [1/M <= u for Wright-Fisher with selection coefficient s >= 0]; Delphi.FavoredChain.fixationProbability_ge [i/M <= u(i) for any favored chain]. Generations available: 4.81e+7 to 9.33e+7 (duration 48.07 to 56 Ma over a generation time of 1 to 0.6 years). Neutral budget, mu T per site (Delphi.neutral_expectedSubstitutions, independent of N): 0.053 to 0.451 substitutions per site, 5.50e+7 to 4.69e+8 genome-wide (G = 1.04e+9); with a 2-year generation time the low end becomes 0.026 per site, and with the next-oldest fossil record in place of the Ypresian one (33.9 Ma, the next-oldest PBDB record (David 1946, fish scales, Late Eocene), used as a sensitivity case if the two Bannikov 2014 Monte Bolca records were set aside) it becomes 0.037 per site. The first appearance rests on 2 PBDB occurrence records from one publication: occ:1364420 Rhamphexocoetus volans, Ypresian 56-48.07 Ma, ref:62285, A. F. Bannikov (2014). The systematic composition of the Eocene actinopterygian fish fauna from Monte Bolca, northern Italy, as known to date.; occ:1364422 Exocoetidae, Ypresian 56-48.07 Ma, ref:62285, the same paper. Floor on adaptive substitutions (Delphi.favored_expectedSubstitutions_ge): mu_f T per site, with mu_f (the rate of mutations selection does not oppose) undefined; it equals the neutral budget at mu_f = mu and is independent of N. Ceiling (Delphi.expectedSubstitutions_le): 2 N mu T per site, N = 1.00e+4: 1.06e+3 to 9.02e+3; N = 1.00e+5: 1.06e+4 to 9.02e+4; N = 1.00e+6: 1.06e+5 to 9.02e+5; N = 1.00e+7: 1.06e+6 to 9.02e+6; N = 1.00e+8: 1.06e+7 to 9.02e+7; N = 1.00e+9: 1.06e+8 to 9.02e+8; vacuous. Required substitutions for a wing: undefined. Verdict: inconclusive. Computed 2026-10-31T23:16:57.558Z by lean/bound/compute.mjs from lean/bound/parameters.json." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/hypothesis/exocoetidae-substitution-budget> ;
    rdfs:comment "This evidence item establishes only that the numbers follow from the named theorems' formulas and the named parameter values. It is not evidence that the parameters are right for Exocoetidae, and not evidence about wings." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/lean.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/4ebb56add61de66744fe8b957ecd7c0bcecc8083/lean/bound/parameters.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/4ebb56add61de66744fe8b957ecd7c0bcecc8083/lean/bound/result.json> .
}

